	(text "STM32L432 USB FS DESIGN:\nUSB_D_P/USB_D_N impedance matching is integrated in the MCU;\nno external series termination resistors are required.\nThe USB_D_P full-speed pull-up is also integrated in the\nSTM32L432, so no external 1.5kΩ pull-up is needed.\n\nUSB data lines shall be routed as a controlled-impedance\n90Ω differential pair. Place the USB ESD protection close\nto the connector and minimize trace length/stubs.\n\nMCU POWER DECOUPLING:\nUsed local ceramic bypass capacitors at the supply pins:\n100 nF at each VDD pin, with an additional 4.7 µF bulk\ncapacitor on the VDD rail. For the VDDA/VREF+ supply,\nused 1 µF + 10 nF to GND. Place the capacitors as close\nas practical to the corresponding MCU pins.\n\nReference: STMicroelectronics AN4879 - USB hardware and\nPCB design guidelines for STM32 MCUs."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 38.862 182.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
				(thickness 0.1588)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0492b36d-1aa8-465f-b484-44459af425a4")
	)
	(text "16V\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 276.352 140.97 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "1975f4a5-1480-4643-a773-479ac4226529")
	)
